# Stage 7 Gelse #1 outrun (D-100 condition, D-085 precedent): the walk-on
# answer to the walkway's Gelse, measured by hand because the solver passes
# before it hunts. As strobl_gelse to deck C (2370), then she waits on the
# deck's left part: Gelse #1 (218, row 8) is fully on screen for 60 frames
# and starts hunting at 2400 (0.75 px/frame per axis, towards her head).
# At 2410 she runs right under it while it is still above her head, jumps
# C -> D off the deck's right end (press 2457, Jumped 2458; the Gelse is
# behind her, ~12 px above her head) and D -> bridge right after landing
# (press 2511), never stomping it; it is still hunting behind her when she
# lands on the Klausbruecke (2556) and drops off the screen's left edge.
# Windows, each press shifted alone with every other input at its frame
# (win.py-style, 2 s after landing): C -> D -3..+7 = 11 frames (earlier
# she jumps into the Gelse: death; later the fixed D -> bridge press comes
# too early: a route limit), D -> bridge -7..+12 = >= 20 (earlier she
# falls short into the gap; +12 = the shift limit). Both >= 5: no gap
# narrowed (the D-100 fallback was not needed). score=8500: the Gelse is
# never stomped (its 100 would show; the earlier Stomped events are
# Selfie-Tourists on the way).
level  = strobl
